      summary: "Written with Aaron Dessner about \"female rage,\" mad woman targets the gaslighting Swift said she felt during her masters dispute — a connection she confirmed herself in a December 2020 interview, comparing the fallout to a divorce.",
      body: ["In a December 2020 Entertainment Weekly interview, Swift confirmed \"mad woman\" (along with \"my tears ricochet\") grew out of her 2019 masters dispute with Scooter Braun and former label boss Scott Borchetta, saying the fallout from the 15-year professional relationship left her \"very triggered by any stories, movies, or narratives revolving from divorce.\" On the song itself, co-written and produced with Aaron Dessner, Swift said its theme of gaslighting was \"the most rage-provoking element of being a female.\""],
