      title: "London Boy opens with Idris Elba's voice, borrowed from James Corden's couch",
      summary: "The album's giddy tour of Camden, Shoreditch, Brixton and Highgate starts with a sampled Idris Elba clip from The Late Late Show — the most gleefully touristy three minutes on Lover.",
      body: ["British listeners immediately pointed out the geography reads like a tourist doing every borough in one afternoon — which became half the song's charm and a running joke online. The London romance at its center went unnamed, but nobody needed a map for that part."],
      tags: ["Music"],
