      id: "vault-midnights-cruel-summer-hits-no-1-four-years-after-it-came-out",
      date: "2023-10-01",
      dateLabel: "October 2023",
      title: "Cruel Summer hits No. 1 — four years after it came out",
      summary: "An unpromoted 2019 album track, revived by the Eras Tour setlist and a viral moment, becomes her 10th Hot 100 No. 1 on the chart dated Oct. 23.",
      body: ["The fifth-longest wait for a No. 1 in Hot 100 history — four years, one month, three weeks after it debuted at No. 29. The final push came from the Eras Tour concert film: the week it hit theaters, the song jumped from No. 9 on 18.6 million streams (up 35%), 41,000 downloads (up 1,482%, juiced by new live and LP Giobbi remix versions released Oct. 18), and 77.8 million in radio audience, taking the chart's Streaming and Sales Gainer honors in the same frame. It made her one of just 11 artists ever to reach ten Hot 100 No. 1s — with a song her label never promoted as a proper single in 2019."],
