      body: ["Opening night on March 13, 2013 drew 13,800 to Omaha's CenturyLink Center — the first of a two-night stand that totaled 27,877 tickets — kicking off a 66-date North American run. Thirteen of the 17 songs came from Red, delivered with a seven-piece band, dancers, pyrotechnics, and more than ten costume changes; the Omaha World-Herald described the crowd's \"screams, whistles and cheers\" melding with the band into \"a relentless cacophony.\" Sheeran, who opened every North American date, came back mid-show to duet \"Everything Has Changed\" with her on the B-stage during the acoustic segment."],
