      summary: "Written from Maya Thompson's blog posts about her son Ronan, who died of neuroblastoma at three — Thompson gets a co-writing credit, and every dollar went to fighting cancer.",
      body: ["Swift debuted the song live at the Stand Up to Cancer telethon on September 8, 2012, and released it as an iTunes-exclusive the same night, with all proceeds donated to cancer charities. She assembled the lyrics from direct quotes in Thompson's blog about her son, crediting her as co-writer. The song later reached No. 16 on the Hot 100 and was certified gold."],
      tags: ["Music"],
