      title: "Call It What You Want closes the arc: rebellion, then falling in love",
      summary: "\"It starts with...rebellion, or anger, or angst...and then falling in love, and realizing you settle into what your priorities are\" — her own map of reputation, with this song as the landing point.",
      body: ["At the same iHeartRadio release-party special, Taylor described how Call It What You Want — track 11, and the one most fans read as being about Joe Alwyn — completes reputation's arc: \"It starts with just getting out any kind of rebellion, or anger, or angst, or whatever. And then, like, falling in love, and realizing that you kind of settle into what your priorities are.\""],
