      date: "2012-02-01",
      dateLabel: "February 2012",
      title: "Mean wins two Grammys the same night",
      summary: "Best Country Song and Best Country Solo Performance at the 54th Grammys — performed live, banjo in hand.",
      body: ["Her reaction caught the full-circle absurdity of it: \"There's no feeling like writing a song about someone who hates you and is mean to you and makes your life miserable ... and then win the Grammy for it.\" She performed the song live at the ceremony and told the room what the night meant — \"It's always gonna mean the world to me, the idea of getting to go to the Grammys\" — on an evening when Speak Now itself was also up for Best Country Album."],
